course: dictionary
lesson: 13450
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer means. The word hotdog is a good example, because it can name a food, describe a show-off, or be a happy shout. «Dad bought two hotdogs at the football game.» Here a hotdog is something you eat: a hot sausage in a soft bread roll.
explain: «Sam loved to hotdog on his skateboard, jumping off every ramp he could find.» Now hotdog is an action word. The clues are skateboard, jumping and every ramp, so it means to show off with daring tricks. This verb is informal and mostly used in the US.
explain: «Hot dog! We won the match!» Here hotdog is a shout of joy, an old-fashioned way of saying great. Test your meaning by swapping in a word: «Great! We won the match!» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Hotdog can be written as one word or as two words, hot dog, and both are correct. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, read the whole sentence, try each meaning, and choose the one that fits the clues.
fact: A hotdog is a hot sausage, usually a frankfurter, served in a long soft bread roll.
fact: Hotdogs are often served with ketchup or mustard, and they are sold at sports games, fairs and barbecues.
fact: As a verb, to hotdog means to show off with daring tricks, for example on skis, a skateboard or a surfboard. It is informal, mainly US.
fact: A hotdog can also be a person who shows off, especially in a sport.
fact: «Hot dog!» is an old-fashioned US shout meaning «great!»
exercise: «Dad bought two hotdogs at the game.» What is a hotdog here? | A ticket for the match | A cold drink with ice | *A hot sausage in a soft bread roll | A small dog that runs very fast
exercise: «Mia tried to hotdog down the big hill on her snowboard.» What does hotdog mean here? | To sleep in the snow | *To show off with daring tricks | To eat a meal on the hill | To wave at the crowd
exercise: «Hot dog! We won the match!» What does the shout hot dog mean? | Hungry | Stop | Cold | *Great
test: «The fair had a hotdog stand by the gate.» What is a hotdog stand? | A stage where a band plays | *A place that sells hot sausages in bread rolls | A place where you learn to skate | A big tent for the animals
test: Jayden says, «Stop hotdogging, you'll fall!» What does hotdogging mean here? | Waiting in a long line | *Showing off with risky tricks | Being very quiet | Eating too fast
exam: Maths: «Each hotdog costs $3. How much do four hotdogs cost?» | $7 | *$12 | $14 | $10
